  "notes": "Describes the dispersal of liquid as a fine mist or spray. Used in agriculture (pesticide spraying), medical settings (disinfection), cosmetics, and cooling systems.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to spray, to atomize\n- ⟦{噴霧器|ふんむき}→噴霧器：25071_funmuki⟧: sprayer, atomizer\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}⟦{消毒|しょうどく}→消毒：07591_shoudoku⟧: spray disinfection\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}{式|しき}: spray-type\n- {噴霧|ふんむ}ノズル: spray nozzle\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦スプレー→スプレー：11581_supuree⟧: spray — the loanword equivalent; more casual and everyday\n- ⟦{散布|さんぷ}→散布：21064_sanpu⟧: scattering, spraying — broader; can include spreading seeds or distributing leaflets, not just liquid\n- ⟦{霧吹|きりふ}き→霧吹き：15171_kirifuki⟧: spray bottle, mister — refers to the handheld tool itself\n\nETYMOLOGY:\n{噴|ふん} (spout, emit) + {霧|む} (mist, fog) — \"emit mist.\"",
